{%- comment -%}
  Block C - prior price.

  The metafield uses Admin API GIDs, whereas Liquid exposes numeric IDs. Keep
  IDs as strings (Shopify IDs can exceed JavaScript's safe integer range).
  The selected variant is rendered server-side; the asset handles later changes.

  Staleness (review finding: "Block C can show a stale prior price"):
  - The stored `show` flag is a hint, never the decision. The block re-checks the
    LIVE compare-at price from the product itself, so when a sale ends and the
    compare-at price is cleared the block hides immediately — even if the
    metafield from the last publish still says `show: true` and still carries the
    old prior price.
  - The stored entry must also describe the price the variant is selling at now.
    A payload written before the latest price change is treated as stale and
    hidden rather than printed.
  - The entry is only ever written with a statutory prior price when the app has
    a complete 30-day lookback (audit L16). A shorter history produces a
    suppressed entry, so the block shows nothing rather than a partial figure
    labelled as though it were the rule's prior price.
  - When the app cannot see a compare-at price on the product at all (some themes
    do not expose it), it falls back to the stored compare_at in the payload, so
    the block still works where the product object is thin.

  Height stability (F4 "no layout shift"):
  - If the product has prior-price data for at least one variant, the block
    always occupies its box. When the selected variant has no prior price the
    stack is hidden with `visibility`, which keeps the reserved space, instead
    of `display: none`, which would pull the page up on a variant switch.
  - `hidden` (no box in the flow at all) is used only when the product has no
    prior-price data for any variant. That is decided server-side and cannot
    change while the merchant switches variants.
  - The label, value and note each have a fixed minimum height in legal-in.css,
    and the note is clamped to two lines, so the two note texts (one line and
    two lines) occupy the same height.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'legal-in.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- liquid
  assign prior = product.metafields.legal_in.prior_price.value
  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign variant_id = current_variant.id | append: ''
  assign variant_gid = 'gid://shopify/ProductVariant/' | append: variant_id
  assign entry = prior.variants | where: 'variant_id', variant_gid | first
  if entry == nil
    assign entry = prior.variants | where: 'variant_id', variant_id | first
  endif

  # The live price of the selected variant, in paise — the unit Shopify uses
  # everywhere in Liquid and in the product JSON. The payload is written in
  # rupees, so the stored figures are converted before they are compared with
  # these (see `entry_price` below). Shopify exposes the price as a number or a
  # decimal string depending on the theme and API version, so it is normalised
  # before use.
  assign live_price = current_variant.price | plus: 0
  assign live_compare = nil
  if current_variant.compare_at_price != blank and current_variant.compare_at_price > 0
    assign live_compare = current_variant.compare_at_price | plus: 0
  endif

  assign show = false
  if entry and entry.prior_price != nil
    # Two ways the stored payload can be stale, and both are checked against the
    # product the theme gave us rather than taken on trust from the metafield:
    #
    #  1. the payload was written for a different selling price (a price edit that
    #     has not been published yet);
    #  2. the live compare-at price is gone or no longer above the selling price,
    #     which is what a sale ending looks like. A blank compare-at price means
    #     "not on sale", NOT "the theme hid it": the block always receives the
    #     full product object from Shopify, so the stored compare-at is never used
    #     to override a live blank one.
    #
    # A payload from before the schema bump carries no prices at all; it was only
    # ever written for reduced variants, so its `show` flag stands in until the
    # next publish rewrites it.
    assign has_stored_prices = false
    if entry.price != blank and entry.compare_at != blank
      assign has_stored_prices = true
    endif

    if has_stored_prices
      assign price_matches = false
      # Rupees in the payload, paise on the product: 249 against 24900 never
      # matched, and the block showed nothing at all on a real store. Convert the
      # stored pair rather than dividing the live one, so both sides stay in the
      # unit Liquid uses and the comparison is exact to the paisa.
      assign entry_price = entry.price | times: 100 | round
      if live_price > 0
        if entry_price == live_price
          assign price_matches = true
        endif
      else
        # The theme handed the block a product without a price: fall back to the
        # stored price rather than hiding a valid prior price.
        assign price_matches = true
      endif

      assign compare_reduced = false
      if live_compare
        if live_compare > live_price
          assign compare_reduced = true
        endif
      elsif live_price <= 0
        # Same thin-product fallback: judge the stored pair, converted the same way.
        assign entry_compare = entry.compare_at | times: 100 | round
        if entry_compare > entry_price
          assign compare_reduced = true
        endif
      endif

      if entry.show and price_matches and compare_reduced
        assign show = true
      endif
    elsif entry.show
      assign show = true
    endif
  endif

  assign prior_cents = entry.prior_price | times: 100
  assign has_any = false
  if prior.variants.size > 0
    assign has_any = true
  endif
-%}
<section
  class="legal-in legal-in--prior-price{% if block.settings.bordered %} legal-in--bordered{% endif %}{% if show %} legal-in--ready{% else %} legal-in--idle{% endif %}"
  data-legal-in-block="prior-price"
  data-variant-id="{{ variant_id | escape }}"
  data-prior="{{ prior | json | escape }}"
  data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
  data-has-prior="{{ has_any }}"
  aria-live="polite"
  {% unless has_any %}hidden{% endunless %}
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="legal-in__stack">
    <p class="legal-in__label">{{ block.settings.heading | default: 'Prior price' | escape }}</p>
    <p class="legal-in__value" data-prior-value>{% if show %}{{ prior_cents | money }}{% endif %}</p>
    <p class="legal-in__note" data-prior-note>
      {%- if show -%}
        Lowest price in the 30 days before the reduction was announced, inclusive of taxes.
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.priorPrice.name",
  "target": "section",
  "javascript": "prior-price.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:blocks.priorPrice.heading.label",
      "default": "Prior price"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "bordered",
      "label": "t:blocks.priorPrice.bordered.label",
      "default": false
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
